:: Millers Babysitting Dinner [nobr]

/* Intro */
As you and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> are hanging out, <span style="color:Yellow">you suddenly notice the time and, on cue, hear the rumbling of <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s tummy.</span> He blushes, looking down at his stomach with a shy smile before saying <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Whoops, guess my belly is getting hungry. Is it dinner time yet?”</span> Seeing as it is around the time <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> mentioned for dinner, you take <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> into the kitchen and began to look around. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Daddy said we’re not allowed to use the oven if he’s not here.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> explains, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“But we have a bunch of microwave dinners. Sometimes <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> makes them for us if daddy is super busy.”</span> He thinks for a moment, looking at the list of instructions and information <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> left on the fridge. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He also said we could order pizza! I’m good with anything as long as I can eat it, so what do you want?”</span> <br>

    <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
        {
            Name: "OC Kayden",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
    ]>>
    <<ad _ad>>

You ponder for a moment, thinking the options over. Sharing a nice, greasy pizza would be nice, but the frozen dinners would be easier and, based on the brands you see in their freezer, <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Hakeem</span> tended to buy the expensive ones that actually taste pretty good! <span style="color:Yellow">It is actually a pretty tough choice.</span> <br><br>

<div id="choice">
    <<link "Pizza<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>

    You decide on pizza and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> jumps up with a cheer. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yay! I love pizza! Oh, what should we get on it? We should get a bunch of meat, I love meat! Daddy said we are little meat goblins since <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> and I love shoving meat in our mouth!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">You nearly choke as <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> says this, the innocent boy not at all getting the lewd implications behind his words. You stifle a laugh as you agree to get plenty of meat for the little meat goblin to shove in his mouth. Maybe, if he’s good, you’ll even give him some of your meat.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yay!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> replies in excitement, still not getting what you mean, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Meat in my mouth! Meat in my mouth!”</span> <span style="color:Pink">The boy begins to do a little dance, pretending to eat long pieces of meat that only add to the lewd undertones. You have a hard time not breaking out laughing as you order the pizza.</span> <br>

            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "OC Kayden",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Everyday",
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> is practically jumping up and down as the pizza is delivered, announcing that he’s ready to <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“shove the meat in my mouth!”</span> to the delivery driver, <span style="color:Pink">who gives you a humorous look of amusement.</span> You make sure to tip him very well and carry the pizza into the kitchen, dividing it in half for you two.<br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> devours his half, before collapsing into a heap on the couch from overeating, groaning with a big belly that he rubs while regretting his choice to eat so much. As he stares at the cartoons, he says <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Uhhggg. So full… I don’t think I can eat anymore.”</span> He looks over at the pizza still on your plate, giving a look of disgust with a hint of desire. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well, maybe if you don’t eat it all you can put it in the fridge. Then maybe I can put your meat in my mouth before bed.”</span> <br>
        <br> 
        <span style="color:LightGreen">You nearly choke on the pizza, telling <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> to maybe avoid describing it like that. The last thing you need is him telling that to <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span> or his father. That would not be an easy thing to explain.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
        <<set $OCKaydenBabysit.State to "PostDin">>
        <span style="color:green">+Kayden Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:green">-Kayden Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 20>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|OC Miller House Kitchen]] 

    <</replace>>
    <</link>>

    <<link "Frozen Dinner<br>">>
    <<replace"#choice">>

        You decide to keep it simple and do a frozen dinner for the two of you. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span> seems happy with this and jumps over to the freezer asking <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Oh! Can I pick out which one I want? I really like the chicken one, but Daddy got us these sausage and egg ones too. They’re not just for breakfast, he said we could have them for dinner too! I love sausages! When <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">ZayZay</span> doesn’t feel like eating, he lets me and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> slurp down his sausage when daddy isn’t looking! His is always saltier than ours though.”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:Pink">You snort loudly at <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Kayden</span>’s words, your image of his and his brother slurping on <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s sausage being a big different than his. You ask if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Isaiah</span>’s sausage is too big of them or just right and he laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nah, it’s normally too small! It’s like a little worm, but one time daddy let <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Jayden</span> and me split his sausage! It was so big we could barely finish it!”</span> You smile, the boy having no idea the lewd images he was putting in your head.</span> <br>
        
            <<set _ad to [
                {
                    Name: "Player",
                    State: {
                        Mouth: "Smirk",
                        Eyes: "Tired",
                        Blush: 1,
                    },
                },
                {
                    Name: "OC Kayden",
                    State: {
                        Outfit: "Everyday",
                        Mouth: "Happy",
                    },
                },
            ]>>
            <<ad _ad>>

        You decide on the breakfast for dinner approach, even pouring some orange juice for the boy. He happily bounces in his seat as he awaits his sausages and, true to what he said, simply slurps them up as he gets them. <span style="color:Pink">You ask what sort of practice he has with that mouth of his, though the boy just looks at you in confusion.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I eat all sorts of stuff with my mouth.”</span> He answers in a slightly confused way, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s a weird question. How else would I eat something?”</span> <br>
        <br>
        <span style="color:LightGreen">You decide to drop the topic for now, finding the teasing too easy and not wanting him to repeat any of this to his father or brothers. That would not be an easy thing to explain.</span> <br>
        <<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
        <<set $OCKaydenBabysit.State to "PostDin">>
        <span style="color:green">+Kayden Fun</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Fun += 10>>
        <span style="color:green">-Kayden Energy</span><br>
        <<set $HangOutNeed.Energy += 20>>
        <br>
        [[Continue|OC Miller House Kitchen]] 

    <</replace>>
    <</link>>
</div>